# Security Recommendations

## Critical

Never trust authorization information stored on the client.

---

## Server-Side Authorization

Store user roles within the server-side session or database.

Example:

```
Session ID
        │
        ▼
Server Session
        │
        ▼
role = administrator
```

---

## Signed Tokens

If authorization data is stored in cookies or JWTs:

- Digitally sign the token.
- Verify the signature on every request.
- Reject any modified values.

---

## Principle of Least Privilege

Every privileged endpoint should independently verify:

- Authentication
- Authorization
- User role

Never rely solely on client-supplied values.

