# Conclusion

The application trusted a client-controlled cookie (`Admin`) to determine authorization privileges.

By intercepting the authentication response and changing the cookie value from `false` to `true`, administrative access was obtained without possessing valid administrator credentials.

This demonstrates why authorization must always be enforced on the server, as any client-side security control can be manipulated by an attacker.

